{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789031332,"nonce":"sLTczd2YhEf5pTd1f9a4x6VlkTs=","message":"Fixed in 5a6bc87.\n\nNot one site but a class. HUI8/HUI16 keep their narrow machine width only in the Cranelift tier, so it is the only one that has to choose a signedness, and it chose signed everywhere:\n\n- coerce() sign-extended on every widening, in both lowerers (14 sites in lower.rs, 29 in codegen.rs). Signedness is now a parameter each site states, taken from the SOURCE's HL kind rather than the destination's.\n- ToSFloat converted with fcvt_from_sint.\n- SDiv/SMod/SShr ran at i16/i8 width on unsigned operands (srem.i16 on a value of 60000).\n- The four signed compare predicates ordered 0x8000..0xFFFF below zero.\n\nThe last two are why the first fix was incomplete: widening correctly still leaves a signed operation at the narrow width.\n\nMeasured against ground truth, 200000 iterations:\n\n              truth      before       after\n  udiv sum    154008793  356314       154008793\n  umod sum    12313449   1888917055   12313449\n  UI16 \u003e      199695     102996       199695\n  UI8  \u003e      159276     65452        159276\n\nThe old behaviour was also NONDETERMINISTIC -- 356314, 3140270 and 35088953 from the same binary -- because promotion timing decided how many iterations ran on the bad lowering. Any past measurement over UI8/UI16 data is suspect, not merely wrong.\n\nRegression test: TestNarrowUnsigned, in the parity smoke list. It checks its own answers and exits non-zero, because the harness compares exit status rather than output, and eval cannot be the oracle (it refuses the hl package). Its expectations are computed in separate Int-only loops on purpose: computing them inline widens the values first and the bug disappears -- the first version of this fixture passed on the broken binary for exactly that reason.\n\nT4 from this issue now reads 144 on every engine and mode, where --mode jit gave -112.","files":null}]}